  <h1>How to download Qwen Chat (chat.qwen.ai) conversations</h1>
  <p class="lead">Qwen Chat is Alibaba's consumer chat product. TotalRecalls reads from your browser session — the DashScope developer API is a different product and is not used.</p>

  <h2>What "download" usually means</h2>
  <p>People searching for this want one of three outcomes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Backup</strong> — don't lose conversations if the account changes</li>
    <li><strong>Multilingual archive</strong> — Chinese, English, Japanese, Korean conversations stay UTF-8 readable</li>
    <li><strong>Searchable library</strong> — find an old answer without scrolling forever</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Option A — Manual copy/paste from chat.qwen.ai</h2>
  <p>Qwen Chat does not provide a built-in data download for chat history. The only manual path is to open each conversation, select the text, and paste it into a local file.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Pros:</strong> no tooling, no install</li>
    <li><strong>Cons:</strong> loses formatting, doesn't scale past a few conversations, easy to lose the order of long ones</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Option B — Local library with TotalRecalls (Windows)</h2>
  <p>TotalRecalls runs on your PC, connects to your Qwen Chat session locally, and writes conversations into folders as Markdown + JSON.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Buy / install TotalRecalls for Windows</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Qwen Chat</strong> as the provider</li>
    <li>Sign in through the local login window at <a href="https://chat.qwen.ai">chat.qwen.ai</a></li>
    <li>Download — files land under <code>Library/qwen/</code></li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Why two Qwen products matter</h2>
  <p>Alibaba ships Qwen two ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Qwen Chat (chat.qwen.ai)</strong> — the consumer chat product. This is what users want to back up.</li>
    <li><strong>DashScope / Bailian / Model Studio (dashscope.aliyuncs.com)</strong> — Alibaba's developer API for the Qwen model family. Has its own ToS rules.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>TotalRecalls only touches the consumer chat product. We never call DashScope endpoints, never use Alibaba API keys, and never touch your developer-account credentials. The download path is the same path a backup tool would use for webmail — read the visible content from your own browser session.</p>

  <h2>Which should you use?</h2>
  <p>Use <strong>manual copy/paste</strong> for one or two conversations you need right now. Use <strong>TotalRecalls</strong> when you want a complete, searchable archive — especially if you also use ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, or Grok and want one archive location for all of them.</p>

  <h2>Tips for a clean Qwen Chat archive</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Run the download while you still have an active session — Qwen Chat sessions expire on inactivity</li>
    <li>Keep the folder inside a backup drive or cloud backup you control</li>
    <li>Prefer Markdown for reading; keep JSON if you might process later</li>
    <li>UTF-8 throughout — Chinese, English, Japanese, Korean all stay readable in any editor</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>About the international vs domestic domain</h2>
  <p>Qwen Chat is served from <code>chat.qwen.ai</code> (international) and from <code>qianwen.com</code> / <code>tongyi.aliyun.com</code> (domestic). TotalRecalls targets the international web app. If you're on the domestic app, sign in via the international one to download.</p>

